# code-is-two-libraries — the SIBLING `code is` library (a vendored sibling) (#198).
library "Two Lib Sub".

// Reached ONLY via `use decision "Two Lib Sub"."Sub Determination"` from main.crl
// (NO explicit `include`), so it is a closure SIBLING, not a seed. Because it ALSO
// declares concept-level `code is` ("Feature Sub"), Option B disambiguates its
// local domain to `<policyId>-<librarySlug>` (`code-is-two-lib-fixture-two-lib-sub`),
// so its local CodeSystem + layered Library identities no longer collide with the
// primary's.

concept "Feature Sub":
- type is Observation.
- code is `feature-sub`.

activity "Refer":
- request CPGCommunicationRequest.
- with `refer`.

decision "Sub Determination":
first:
- when "Feature Sub" then recommend activity "Refer".
- otherwise then recommend activity "Refer".
